      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "Feel the two-pace horses will dominate up front. The up-and-comer is COAL RIVER (2) who is racing well including a last-start all-the-way win at Hobart. Into open class now but drops 4.5kg and in the small field will take catching. SUSHI EXPRESS (1) will be pushing forward as well and looks the toughest to beat. Unbeaten from two tries this course and distance and proven in this class. Will be in it for a long way. THE LONGEST YARD (5) has a good record at this course and distance and drops in the weights for this. Suited by the extra ground and should be tough to stop. GARCON D'ESPOIR (6) is long overdue for a win after a string of placings and sure to measure up again. CAPTAIN CAM (4) kept coming here last time and did win only try this trip.",
